      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T12:17:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "args4j allows to express option dependencies declaratively.\nE.g.\n```\n    @Option(name \u003d \"--foo\", usage \u003d \"This is option foo. If present, --bar is required.\")\n    private boolean foo;\n\n    @Option(name \u003d \"--bar\", usage \u003d \"This is option bar.\", depends \u003d {\"--foo\"})\n    private boolean bar;\n```\n\nargs4j also has a `forbids` attribute if you need to specify options that cannot be used together. For instance, `@Option(name\u003d\"-foo\", forbids\u003d{\"--baz\"})` would prevent `--foo` and `--baz` from being used simultaneously.",
